WEBVTT

00:00:01.040 --> 00:00:02.980
﻿Sei. Reiji.

00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:07.750
﻿The Gunpla that interfered
﻿with your race was controlled by...

00:00:08.520 --> 00:00:11.090
﻿a Gunpla mafia guy called "C".

00:00:12.020 --> 00:00:14.260
﻿Gunpla mafia?

00:00:14.660 --> 00:00:15.720
﻿Who are they?

00:00:16.460 --> 00:00:22.060
﻿They're underworld types who'll
﻿take any dirty job for money.

00:00:23.030 --> 00:00:26.870
﻿Whoever hired this guy
﻿must be after you two.

00:00:28.170 --> 00:00:32.070
﻿That Mega Size Model Zaku
﻿that barged into the Battle Royale...

00:00:33.010 --> 00:00:37.350
﻿It also seemed to be
﻿deliberately targeting us.

00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:39.080
﻿But why?

00:00:39.080 --> 00:00:41.280
﻿We haven't done anything wrong.

00:00:41.280 --> 00:00:42.680
﻿I heard that Zaku...

00:00:42.690 --> 00:00:47.890
﻿was sent in by the organizer
﻿to spice up the battle.

00:00:49.630 --> 00:00:50.930
﻿Reiji?

00:00:50.930 --> 00:00:51.790
﻿Where're you going?

00:00:52.530 --> 00:00:54.730
﻿I have some business to take care of.

00:00:54.730 --> 00:00:57.470
﻿Sei, I'm leaving the Gunpla to you.

00:00:59.500 --> 00:01:00.800
What!!!???

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:04.240
﻿H-How did you get in?

00:01:04.570 --> 00:01:07.140
﻿I asked them to let me in.

00:01:07.640 --> 00:01:09.580
﻿Very gently and politely.

00:01:09.680 --> 00:01:12.650
﻿A-And what do you want from me?

00:01:13.450 --> 00:01:16.790
﻿Are you the one who's been
﻿interfering with our matches!?

00:01:18.120 --> 00:01:20.120
﻿Th-That gem...!

00:01:20.960 --> 00:01:23.790
﻿Just as I thought, this boy is...

00:01:24.730 --> 00:01:27.900
﻿The crown prince of Arian...!

00:02:59.130 --> 00:03:01.600
﻿I-It's a misunderstanding, Mr. Reiji.

00:03:01.870 --> 00:03:08.210
﻿S-Sure, I'm the main sponsor and
﻿head of the organizing company, but...

00:03:08.210 --> 00:03:10.810
﻿I'm not directly involved
﻿in running the tournament.

00:03:10.810 --> 00:03:12.980
﻿I would never interfere with—

00:03:13.080 --> 00:03:15.380
﻿But the fact is, we're being attacked!

00:03:15.380 --> 00:03:17.890
﻿Th-That's unforgivable.

00:03:17.890 --> 00:03:20.520
﻿I'll have the administration side
﻿look into it at once,

00:03:20.520 --> 00:03:22.960
﻿and reinforce the security.

00:03:23.860 --> 00:03:27.030
﻿Mr. Reiji,
﻿we caused you some trouble.

00:03:27.030 --> 00:03:30.030
﻿I must apologize as the organizer.

00:03:30.730 --> 00:03:32.100
﻿I'm sorry.

00:03:34.100 --> 00:03:37.270
﻿Really, I'm so sorry!

00:03:39.910 --> 00:03:42.740
﻿Personally, I don't care.

00:03:42.740 --> 00:03:44.150
﻿Huh?

00:03:44.150 --> 00:03:46.610
﻿Whether there's
﻿interference or meddlers,

00:03:46.620 --> 00:03:48.480
﻿I'll accept any challenge.

00:03:49.180 --> 00:03:50.080
﻿But...

00:03:50.590 --> 00:03:54.890
﻿If anyone messes with the people
﻿giving their all in this tournament...

00:03:56.390 --> 00:03:59.330
﻿No matter who it is,

00:03:59.330 --> 00:04:01.430
﻿I won't show any mercy.

00:04:08.870 --> 00:04:10.870
﻿We're 17th in the qualifiers.

00:04:11.040 --> 00:04:13.970
﻿To get into the best 16
﻿and advance to the finals,

00:04:14.380 --> 00:04:17.580
﻿we have to nail the final period
﻿that starts tomorrow.

00:04:19.410 --> 00:04:21.220
﻿We've got to win.

00:04:22.820 --> 00:04:25.890
﻿I'm... I'm scared, Baker.

00:04:26.220 --> 00:04:29.020
﻿Don't worry anymore, Chairman.

00:04:29.020 --> 00:04:31.960
﻿I-I mean, that boy...

00:04:31.960 --> 00:04:34.900
﻿It seems he doesn't remember for now,

00:04:34.900 --> 00:04:37.060
﻿but he could recall everything.

00:04:37.070 --> 00:04:38.830
﻿Recall what?

00:04:40.340 --> 00:04:42.500
﻿My secret.

00:04:42.500 --> 00:04:44.870
﻿And that of the Plavsky particle—

00:04:50.010 --> 00:04:51.080
﻿What's wrong?

00:04:52.710 --> 00:04:54.820
﻿I'm sorry, sir.

00:04:54.820 --> 00:04:56.420
﻿It was just my imagination.

00:04:56.420 --> 00:04:58.520
﻿D-Don't scare me!

00:04:59.650 --> 00:05:01.890
﻿Just as I thought.

00:05:01.890 --> 00:05:07.190
﻿PPSE's Chairman Mashita knows
﻿the secret of creating Plavsky particles.

00:05:08.060 --> 00:05:12.100
﻿But why is it so confidential?

00:05:21.980 --> 00:05:23.610
﻿Meijin,

00:05:23.610 --> 00:05:27.110
﻿the final period rules
﻿and matchups are set.

00:05:28.480 --> 00:05:31.520
﻿They'll be one-on-one battles.

00:05:31.520 --> 00:05:35.090
﻿You opponent is Khalifa,
﻿representing Oman.

00:05:35.090 --> 00:05:37.090
﻿Never heard of him.

00:05:37.090 --> 00:05:40.090
﻿There's no need
﻿to remember a loser's name.

00:05:40.100 --> 00:05:42.130
﻿Just win.

00:05:42.130 --> 00:05:44.730
﻿Yeah, you're right.

00:05:45.300 --> 00:05:48.470
By the way,
﻿I found one interesting match.

00:05:53.410 --> 00:05:54.580
﻿No way.

00:05:55.380 --> 00:05:58.950
﻿Mr. Fellini's our next opponent?

00:06:01.750 --> 00:06:03.120
﻿That's exciting.

00:06:03.820 --> 00:06:07.220
﻿We'll finally be able to
﻿battle with Fellini for real.

00:06:07.890 --> 00:06:11.660
﻿But if you lose, you guys will—

00:06:11.660 --> 00:06:14.630
﻿Don't say negative things like that.

00:06:14.630 --> 00:06:15.400
﻿Right, Sei?

00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:17.400
﻿Y-Yeah.

00:06:19.830 --> 00:06:21.200
﻿Exactly!

00:06:21.200 --> 00:06:22.600
﻿We're gonna win!

00:06:24.240 --> 00:06:25.570
﻿Mr. Fellini!

00:06:27.740 --> 00:06:30.240
﻿He's all ready for battle.

00:06:32.850 --> 00:06:35.620
﻿I'm getting fired up.

00:07:15.390 --> 00:07:18.560
﻿This should take me
﻿to the tournament finals.

00:07:56.200 --> 00:07:58.800
﻿Old man Luang did it, too!

00:07:58.800 --> 00:08:03.300
﻿Now he's got a ticket
﻿to the tournament finals.

00:08:03.810 --> 00:08:05.770
﻿Make sure to follow him, Reiji.

00:08:06.610 --> 00:08:08.080
﻿Of course.

00:08:08.080 --> 00:08:10.340
﻿Iori didn't come to watch?

00:08:10.350 --> 00:08:12.980
﻿He's in the room prepping
﻿the Star Build Strike.

00:08:13.820 --> 00:08:18.550
﻿He's concentrating so hard
﻿I'm afraid to talk to him.

00:08:31.130 --> 00:08:34.370
﻿Is this seat taken, Senorita?

00:08:35.400 --> 00:08:37.240
﻿Oh, Mr. Fellini.

00:08:37.240 --> 00:08:39.410
﻿Huh? Have we met before?

00:08:41.340 --> 00:08:43.040
﻿What're you saying?

00:08:43.040 --> 00:08:44.340
﻿It's me.

00:08:44.610 --> 00:08:46.350
﻿K-Kirara!?

00:08:47.420 --> 00:08:48.720
﻿You couldn't tell?

00:08:49.020 --> 00:08:49.950
﻿What!?

00:08:49.950 --> 00:08:52.150
﻿Um... Of course I knew.

00:08:52.620 --> 00:08:55.360
﻿How could I not tell?

00:08:55.360 --> 00:08:56.590
﻿Whatever.

00:09:00.530 --> 00:09:05.070
﻿Anyway, congratulations on
﻿passing the qualifiers.

00:09:07.800 --> 00:09:08.940
﻿Grazie.

00:09:12.370 --> 00:09:13.910
﻿It's impressive.

00:09:13.910 --> 00:09:18.110
﻿You made it to the finals even
﻿before tomorrow's match.

00:09:19.810 --> 00:09:22.480
﻿Yeah, tell me about it.

00:09:23.380 --> 00:09:26.490
﻿So you can lose for them
﻿tomorrow without hesitation.

00:09:26.490 --> 00:09:27.020
What?

00:09:28.220 --> 00:09:29.860
﻿Am I wrong?

00:09:29.860 --> 00:09:34.130
﻿After the first day, 14 fighters
﻿have passed the qualifiers.

00:09:34.130 --> 00:09:38.300
﻿Your favorite team of
﻿Sei Iori and Reiji are 17th.

00:09:38.870 --> 00:09:40.930
﻿If you lose for them,

00:09:40.940 --> 00:09:43.940
﻿then you can all go
﻿to the tournament finals.

00:09:43.940 --> 00:09:45.370
﻿That's your plan, right?

00:09:47.780 --> 00:09:49.410
﻿Huh? It's not?

00:09:49.410 --> 00:09:50.740
﻿What?

00:09:50.750 --> 00:09:52.150
﻿How did you know?

00:09:53.080 --> 00:09:55.080
﻿That's our Fellini!

00:10:05.830 --> 00:10:08.500
﻿The Star Build Strike Gundam.

00:10:09.160 --> 00:10:12.470
﻿A shield that absorbs
﻿the opponent's particle beams...

00:10:12.470 --> 00:10:16.140
﻿And a system that uses the
﻿absorbed particles for its own output.

00:10:16.940 --> 00:10:19.940
﻿It's amazing he built
﻿such a Gunpla in so little time.

00:10:21.880 --> 00:10:23.510
﻿No.

00:10:23.780 --> 00:10:26.480
﻿He had that potential from the beginning.

00:10:27.150 --> 00:10:30.920
﻿By partnering with Reiji
﻿and fighting all those strong opponents,

00:10:31.720 --> 00:10:35.090
﻿Sei Iori's building ability
﻿finally awakened.

00:10:36.220 --> 00:10:39.430
﻿And who knows how it will evolve?

00:10:44.670 --> 00:10:48.400
﻿Going head-to-head with it
﻿would be costly.

00:10:48.400 --> 00:10:52.940
﻿I could lose on purpose and
﻿spare my machine for the finals.

00:10:53.980 --> 00:10:56.910
﻿Besides, I'm fighting Sei and Reiji.

00:10:56.910 --> 00:10:59.350
﻿Part of me wants to let them win.

00:11:03.250 --> 00:11:06.750
﻿But that's just not me.

00:11:09.890 --> 00:11:13.430
﻿That isn't like
﻿the Italian champ, Ricardo Fellini.

00:11:14.560 --> 00:11:17.630
﻿Right, Fenice?

00:11:24.540 --> 00:11:25.970
<i>﻿Funnels!</i>

00:11:36.280 --> 00:11:37.820
﻿They must be transparent!

00:11:43.290 --> 00:11:44.990
<i>﻿Battle ended.</i>

00:11:59.510 --> 00:12:02.580
﻿Mr. Ral, where were you?

00:12:02.580 --> 00:12:03.610
﻿I was on patrol.

00:12:03.980 --> 00:12:05.050
﻿Huh?

00:12:05.050 --> 00:12:07.810
﻿Oh, nothing. Don't worry.

00:12:07.820 --> 00:12:09.520
﻿What about their battle?

00:12:10.050 --> 00:12:11.750
﻿It's about to begin.

00:12:23.530 --> 00:12:25.570
- ﻿Let's go.
- ﻿Yeah.

00:12:27.740 --> 00:12:31.370
﻿We will now begin match 26
﻿of the eighth period.

00:12:31.940 --> 00:12:37.540
<i>﻿A Gunpla battle of
﻿Sei Iori and Reiji versus Ricardo Fellini!</i>

00:12:40.450 --> 00:12:41.310
﻿Aren't you leaving?

00:12:42.620 --> 00:12:44.720
﻿Allow me to watch this battle.

00:12:44.720 --> 00:12:48.520
﻿It's rare that
﻿you show interest in a battle.

00:12:49.190 --> 00:12:51.390
<i>﻿Please set your GP Base.</i>

00:12:59.300 --> 00:13:02.200
<i>﻿Beginning Plavsky particle dispersal.</i>

00:13:05.570 --> 00:13:08.040
<i>﻿Field 9, Canyon.</i>

00:13:17.820 --> 00:13:18.790
<i>﻿Battle start.</i>

00:13:21.590 --> 00:13:23.920
﻿- Star Build Strike!
- ﻿Let's go!

00:13:25.830 --> 00:13:28.100
﻿Wing Gundam Fenice, here I come!

00:13:36.700 --> 00:13:37.770
﻿He's not firing at us?

00:13:38.410 --> 00:13:40.470
﻿He's wary of our Absorb Shield.

00:13:41.710 --> 00:13:43.940
- <i>That's not all.</i>
- Huh?

00:13:45.280 --> 00:13:47.050
<i>﻿He wants to greet us first!</i>

00:13:51.920 --> 00:13:53.120
﻿We're going to collide!

00:14:02.360 --> 00:14:03.600
<i>﻿Fellini.</i>

00:14:05.430 --> 00:14:06.900
<i>﻿I accept...</i>

00:14:06.900 --> 00:14:08.440
...your resolve!

00:14:17.250 --> 00:14:18.080
<i>﻿What!?</i>

00:14:19.150 --> 00:14:20.450
<i>﻿Where're you looking?</i>

00:14:30.560 --> 00:14:32.460
﻿- The shield!
﻿- How dare you...

00:14:35.000 --> 00:14:36.360
﻿Why?

00:14:36.860 --> 00:14:38.570
﻿How come...?

00:14:38.570 --> 00:14:40.300
﻿Aren't you letting them win?

00:14:40.840 --> 00:14:42.700
﻿Fellini...

00:15:02.290 --> 00:15:03.460
﻿That wasn't good enough.

00:15:03.890 --> 00:15:04.720
﻿What!?

00:15:06.330 --> 00:15:09.130
﻿I taught you to make use of
﻿the terrain, didn't I?

00:15:15.370 --> 00:15:16.240
﻿The booster!

00:15:21.240 --> 00:15:24.310
﻿As I thought,
﻿the Star Build Strike is losing.

00:15:24.980 --> 00:15:29.420
﻿Sei Iori's Gunpla has
﻿slightly better performance, but...

00:15:29.420 --> 00:15:34.250
﻿as a fighter, Mr. Fellini has
﻿vastly more experience.

00:15:34.390 --> 00:15:36.460
﻿Think again.

00:15:36.460 --> 00:15:40.130
﻿Sei's knowledge of Gundam stories...

00:15:40.130 --> 00:15:42.860
﻿more than makes up
﻿for Reiji's inexperience.

00:15:51.440 --> 00:15:52.010
<i>﻿There!</i>

00:15:52.370 --> 00:15:53.270
<i>﻿Gotcha!</i>

00:15:55.340 --> 00:15:55.840
﻿What!?

00:16:06.390 --> 00:16:07.790
<i>﻿It's going to explode!</i>

00:16:09.860 --> 00:16:10.460
<i>﻿You're mine!</i>

00:16:15.230 --> 00:16:16.730
﻿Darn you!

00:16:36.150 --> 00:16:38.950
﻿The Star Build Strike...

00:16:46.890 --> 00:16:50.460
﻿Does it hurt, Fenice?

00:16:51.830 --> 00:16:53.400
﻿I'm sorry.

00:16:54.570 --> 00:17:01.070
﻿But I didn't build you to
﻿be put on a shelf for display.

00:17:04.680 --> 00:17:06.150
﻿I built you to win!

00:17:16.190 --> 00:17:18.330
﻿The Gunpla I made...

00:17:20.760 --> 00:17:22.860
﻿My Wing Gundam Fenice...

00:17:24.470 --> 00:17:28.900
﻿I made you to show the world
﻿that you're the strongest!

00:17:33.840 --> 00:17:35.810
﻿So...

00:17:36.110 --> 00:17:38.710
﻿Just hang in there a little longer.

00:17:41.980 --> 00:17:42.880
﻿Okay, partner?

00:17:45.950 --> 00:17:48.990
﻿Let's grab victory with these hands!

00:17:56.560 --> 00:18:00.070
﻿Reiji, use the RG System in full mode.

00:18:01.400 --> 00:18:03.040
﻿You sure, Sei?

00:18:03.040 --> 00:18:07.370
﻿If we use it in this condition,
﻿the Star Build Strike will...

00:18:07.380 --> 00:18:10.610
<i>﻿Mr. Fellini means to win the battle,</i>

00:18:10.610 --> 00:18:12.180
<i>﻿even if he loses the Fenice.</i>

00:18:14.150 --> 00:18:15.980
﻿To win against him,

00:18:15.980 --> 00:18:20.920
﻿the Star Build Strike and I
﻿need to have the same resolve!

00:18:27.500 --> 00:18:29.000
﻿That light...!

00:18:29.330 --> 00:18:33.570
﻿By having Plavsky particles
﻿permeate it both inside and out,

00:18:33.800 --> 00:18:37.840
﻿they can control the Gunpla better
﻿and maximize the machine's output.

00:18:38.640 --> 00:18:41.510
﻿This is the true power
﻿of the Star Build Strike!

00:18:42.710 --> 00:18:44.940
﻿This is Iori's...

00:18:46.110 --> 00:18:48.350
﻿This is Reiji's Gunpla..

00:18:54.560 --> 00:18:56.760
﻿- Let's go, Sei!
- ﻿Yeah!

00:19:01.130 --> 00:19:01.800
﻿It's fast!

00:19:28.290 --> 00:19:29.460
﻿The strain's too much!

00:19:29.890 --> 00:19:30.560
﻿Just do it!

00:19:44.940 --> 00:19:47.570
﻿Why is he doing all this?

00:19:47.580 --> 00:19:51.510
﻿Mr. Fellini already
﻿has a spot in the finals.

00:19:52.410 --> 00:19:53.610
﻿Don't you get it?

00:19:54.980 --> 00:19:57.150
﻿Meijin Kawaguchi?

00:19:57.150 --> 00:20:00.920
﻿You don't seem to
﻿be a big fan of Gunpla.

00:20:01.590 --> 00:20:03.390
﻿Then watch closely.

00:20:06.060 --> 00:20:09.400
﻿Watch this battle
﻿between true Gunpla Fighters!

00:20:25.480 --> 00:20:27.480
﻿Go, Reiji!

00:20:27.680 --> 00:20:30.380
﻿You're finished now!

00:20:30.620 --> 00:20:33.320
﻿I won't lose!

00:20:53.940 --> 00:20:55.180
<i>﻿Battle ended.</i>

00:21:01.120 --> 00:21:05.450
<i>﻿The result of this battle is a draw.</i>

00:21:35.020 --> 00:21:38.180
﻿Sorry, Star Build Strike.

00:21:41.390 --> 00:21:43.360
﻿Thank you.

00:23:14.010 --> 00:23:16.680
﻿Th-Th-They got through the qualifiers!?

00:23:16.950 --> 00:23:17.920
﻿Yes.

00:23:17.920 --> 00:23:22.490
﻿Sei Iori and Reiji earned
﻿two points for a draw,

00:23:22.490 --> 00:23:25.060
﻿and made it to the finals in 16th place.

00:23:26.290 --> 00:23:29.260
﻿How could that happen!?

00:23:29.830 --> 00:23:32.070
﻿Sei, can I borrow your pin vise?

00:23:33.300 --> 00:23:34.730
﻿The 0.5mm drill.

00:23:36.140 --> 00:23:37.670
﻿Would you like some sandpaper?

00:23:37.810 --> 00:23:39.570
﻿Yeah. #800, please.

00:23:40.610 --> 00:23:43.080
﻿To think you guys beat
﻿each other up yesterday.

00:23:47.150 --> 00:23:50.880
﻿Is Gunpla building really that fun?

00:23:51.720 --> 00:23:54.850
﻿Sure it is!

00:23:56.040 --> 00:23:57.870
﻿I met this strange guy in town.

00:23:57.870 --> 00:23:59.640
﻿Could he be...?

00:23:59.790 --> 00:24:01.880
Next episode, "Dad, We Meet Again?".

00:24:01.880 --> 00:24:04.940
How could a parent not love their child?
